{"name":"Flaming Torch","hex":"#d2864e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flaming","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["On fire with visible flames.","Very bright and the color of flame."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of flame"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flaming"},{"term":"torch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stick of wood or plant fibres twisted together, with one end soaked in a flammable substance such as resin or tallow and set on fire, which is held in the hand, put into a wall bracket, or stuck into the ground, and used chiefly as a light source.","A similarly shaped implement with a replaceable supply of flammable material; specifically, a pole with a lamp at one end."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To illuminate or provide (a place) with torches (noun etymology 1, noun sense 1).\n To intentionally destroy (something) by setting it on fire, especially when committing arson in furtherance of some other criminal act (e.g. insurance fraud or the destruction of evidence).","To illuminate or provide (a place) with torches (noun etymology 1, noun sense 1)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/torch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Billbergia pyramidalis","blocks":[{"text":"Billbergia pyramidalis, commonly known as the flaming torch and foolproof plant, is a species of bromeliad that is native to northern South America and parts of the Caribbean. It was first described by John Sims, and got its current name by John Lindley."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Billbergia_pyramidalis_in_Hyderabad_Nursery_W_IMG_0425.jpg/330px-Billbergia_pyramidalis_in_Hyderabad_Nursery_W_IMG_0425.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billbergia_pyramidalis"},{"title":"Torch","blocks":[{"text":"A torch is a stick with combustible material at one end which can be used 